WEBVTT

00:01:58.704 --> 00:02:01.663
who is to be exchanged
against goods and services.

00:02:01.663 --> 00:02:04.329
If the total amount
of currency in circulation

00:02:04.329 --> 00:02:07.163
increases faster than
the total value of goods and services

00:02:07.163 --> 00:02:08.163
in the economy,

00:02:08.163 --> 00:02:09.621
then each ticket will allow

00:02:09.621 --> 00:02:12.746
buy a smaller portion
of these things than before.

00:02:12.746 --> 00:02:14.371
We call it inflation.

00:02:14.371 --> 00:02:15.454
On another side,

00:02:15.454 --> 00:02:17.663
if the money contribution
remains the same,

00:02:17.663 --> 00:02:20.038
while more goods
and services are produced,

00:02:20.038 --> 00:02:24.788
the value of every dollar would increase
in a process called deflation.

00:02:24.788 --> 00:02:26.246
So which one is the worst?

00:02:26.246 --> 00:02:29.371
Too much inflation means that 
the money in your wallet today

00:02:29.371 --> 00:02:30.996
will be worth less tomorrow,